                        ],
                        "form": "stoïschere"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "dc45e585-7a31-4073-b1b0-de8b76b1e2d9",
                        "entry_id": "11957797-b4ae-32a1-8a9e-3ed7ab2e6bac",
                        "tags": [
                            "partitive",
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "stoïschers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "899b2c2e-99f7-3035-acb0-40d4dc6ed78a",
                        "entry_id": "11957797-b4ae-32a1-8a9e-3ed7ab2e6bac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "op de wijze van een stoïcijn"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "abbba040-f682-4ee3-9905-5a36bc82198b",
                                "sense_id": "899b2c2e-99f7-3035-acb0-40d4dc6ed78a",
                                "text": "In de vroege Romeinse keizertijd sloten aristocraten zichzelf onder invloed van de stoïsche filosofie soms expres een tijdlang op in een sober kamertje, om zich te oefenen in eenzaamheid en armoede."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8899ca92-1089-491a-9127-6d33bc793b5b",
                                "sense_id": "899b2c2e-99f7-3035-acb0-40d4dc6ed78a",
                                "text": "Steek ook maar het Zakboekje van Epictetus bij je, want dat bevat wenken voor een ‘juiste houding in uiteenlopende situaties’. Epictetus was een stoïsche wijsgeer uit de eerste eeuw na Christus."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0df33265-dfce-46d7-a4a0-6aed6ad313cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "11957797-b4ae-32a1-8a9e-3ed7ab2e6bac",
                        "source_sense_id": "899b2c2e-99f7-3035-acb0-40d4dc6ed78a",
                        "source_sense_description": "berustend, gevoelloos",
                        "target_lang_word": "stoical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stoical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aacc8c91-a7d7-3886-acf3-6e174c61ae9d",
                                        "entry_id": "0f2ff8aa-c7a4-39a8-8863-bf340379e3df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Enduring pain and hardship without showing feeling or complaint."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3703454e-c5c9-4b6f-aebd-6ceb7079bec5",
                                                "sense_id": "aacc8c91-a7d7-3886-acf3-6e174c61ae9d",
                                                "text": "\"More and more, the shrewdest thinkers and artists are precocious archeologists of ... ruins-in-the-making, indignant or stoical diagnosticians of defeat, enigmatic choreographers of the complex spiritual movements useful for individual survival in an era or permanent apocalypse.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9ba5fa67-7d4f-4a4b-aae2-33a7983606b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "11957797-b4ae-32a1-8a9e-3ed7ab2e6bac",
                        "source_sense_id": "899b2c2e-99f7-3035-acb0-40d4dc6ed78a",
                        "source_sense_description": "berustend, gevoelloos",
                        "target_lang_word": "stoic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stoic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "daa812fd-920b-33cd-b1d5-511347bcbf2e",
                                        "entry_id": "c70da862-b38f-3aec-be17-23b067f40d75",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Proponent of stoicism, a school of thought, from in 300 B.C.E. up to about the time of Marcus Aurelius, who holds that by cultivating an understanding of the logos, or natural law, one can be free of suffering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8df61ca6-657f-4511-a1d1-3d76e15c93bc",
                                                "sense_id": "daa812fd-920b-33cd-b1d5-511347bcbf2e",
                                                "text": "The anima mundi, to whose disposal of his own personal destiny the Stoic consents, is there to be respected and submitted to, but the Christian God is there to be loved; and the difference of emotional atmosphere is like that between an arctic climate and the tropics, though the outcome in the way of accepting actual conditions uncomplainingly may seem in abstract terms to be much the same."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6272d90f-f2b0-3d65-8e50-8fcf2fca1d42",
                                        "entry_id": "c70da862-b38f-3aec-be17-23b067f40d75",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person indifferent to pleasure or pain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94e5b74b-f5a9-40df-b89d-ab6fcaacd195",
                                                "sense_id": "6272d90f-f2b0-3d65-8e50-8fcf2fca1d42",
                                                "text": "Even a Rolls-Royce owner, I began to feel, would be a stoic to travel across Europe by car when the \"Rheingold\" is on offer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "stoic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88e5006c-b394-392b-b491-f23f1bd888a8",
                                        "entry_id": "086edcd8-8b2e-3581-abee-f6f8822050ba",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to the Stoics or their ideas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1069590f-e8ab-319d-baa7-51c0dd3b02f8",
                                        "entry_id": "086edcd8-8b2e-3581-abee-f6f8822050ba",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not affected by pain or distress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0cd819a-cb08-3ada-8e4b-20d107a711e9",
                                        "entry_id": "086edcd8-8b2e-3581-abee-f6f8822050ba",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not displaying any external signs of being affected by pain or distress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a92c896c-fc52-4ebe-a9f4-c09e2b846dd7",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cd819a-cb08-3ada-8e4b-20d107a711e9",
                                                "text": "It makes a tremendous emotional and practical difference to one whether one accept the universe in the drab discolored way of stoic resignation to necessity, or with the passionate happiness of Christian saints."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
